# DTF tier manifest: auth-strictness-1120
#   (artifact-keeper 1.12.0 auth strictness fixes: #5525, #5482, #5259)
# Profile-set: filesystem + sso.mock-ci-oidc (the CI OIDC issuer of the
# ci-oidc-exchange tier, minting RS256 assertions with claims the oracle
# picks) + sso.ldap (osixia LDAPS). sso.ldap is listed last so its
# AK_SSRF_ALLOW_PRIVATE_CIDRS (which includes 172.16.0.0/12) wins.
#
# RED image: main sha-c3a650e (2026-11-03, before #5261, #5520 and #5797).
# 1.11.13 carries #5520, so it is not red for #5525.
# GREEN: main carrying all three fixes (sha-2bdf092 or later).
#
# CONTROLS (pass on every image)
#   a wrong ASCII Basic password on a private PyPI simple index is 401 and the
#   admin's Basic login is 200; a signed CI assertion with iss and aud is
#   exchanged (with and without provider_id) and a wrong aud is 401; an LDAP
#   user logs in through an enabled provider, and a disabled provider leaves
#   GET /auth/sso/providers; an ordinary API route carries Referrer-Policy
#   strict-origin-when-cross-origin and the Agent Plugins token-in-path route
#   answers 200 with Cache-Control private, no-store.
#
# FIX CASES (RED on sha-c3a650e)
#   #5525 Basic 'x:1234567é' (é across byte 8) on /pypi/{repo}/simple/ is 401;
#     red: the token lookup panics on a byte-index slice and the connection
#     drops (curl exit 52).
#   #5482 a signed CI assertion with no aud, aud null or aud 42 is 401, and one
#     with no iss sent with {provider_id} is 401; red: 200 with a token.
#     LDAP login through a disabled provider is 404 with no token; red: 200.
#     (The blank-sub OIDC callback facet needs a scripted OIDC IdP and is left
#     to the backend's sso_oidc_login_callback_e2e_tests.)
#   #5259 the Agent Plugins token route keeps Referrer-Policy: no-referrer;
#     red: the global layer overwrote it with strict-origin-when-cross-origin.
#
# Secrets: the LDAP user's password is generated at run time; the overlay's
# throwaway bind password is assembled, not committed.
COVERS="5525 5482 5259"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem sso.mock-ci-oidc sso.ldap"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
